        "@value": "allow AI update"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#InnovationFamily",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A named analytical abstraction grouping multiple specific innovation\n    implementations by shared mechanism, feature dimensions, or functional domain.\n    NOT a taxonomy class or SKOS concept: families are dynamic named entities with\n    temporal identity, split/merge history, and family-level analytics.\n    They are the unit of analysis; innovations are the unit of information."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "No close equivalent in standard\n    ontologies. Conceptually analogous to a product family in manufacturing\n    ontologies but InnovationFamily groups genuinely distinct implementations,\n    not variants of one product. schema:ProductGroup is NOT used (see v0.6\n    alignment rationale). Custom class in the sti_atio: namespace."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Innovation Family"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://schema.org/Thing"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#allowsAIEnrichment",
